# Caddy reverse proxy config for ppsl.net.in.
#
# TLS here uses a static Cloudflare Origin Certificate, NOT Caddy's
# automatic Let's Encrypt / ACME management. That switch was necessary
# because ppsl.net.in's DNS record is proxied through Cloudflare
# (orange-cloud): confirmed live on this server, Caddy's automatic HTTPS
# retried for 12+ hours and could not succeed, because Cloudflare's edge
# - not this origin - is what the public internet actually reaches on
# ports 80/443 for a proxied record, which structurally blocks both ACME
# challenge types:
#   - http-01: the plaintext challenge request never reaches Caddy's
#     solver the way ACME expects; Let's Encrypt's validator got back
#     the frontend's own HTML instead of the challenge token.
#   - tls-alpn-01: fails outright ("Cannot negotiate ALPN protocol
#     acme-tls/1"), since Cloudflare's edge answers the TLS handshake
#     itself and doesn't forward that negotiation through to Caddy.
#
# The fix: generate a Cloudflare Origin Certificate instead (Cloudflare
# dashboard > SSL/TLS > Origin Server > Create Certificate - valid for up
# to 15 years, no ACME challenge involved at all) and give Caddy that
# cert/key directly. Cloudflare's edge already trusts its own Origin CA,
# so with SSL/TLS mode set to Full (strict) in the Cloudflare dashboard,
# every hop end-to-end (browser<->Cloudflare, Cloudflare<->this origin)
# is a real, currently-valid certificate.
#
# The cert/key files themselves are NOT in this repo (see docker-compose.yml
# - they're bind-mounted from ./caddy_certs on the server, gitignored,
# same treatment as .env) - place them there directly on the server:
#   caddy_certs/ppsl_net_in.pem   (the "Origin Certificate" Cloudflare gives you)
#   caddy_certs/ppsl_net_in.key   (the "Private Key" Cloudflare gives you - keep this secret)
#
# Everything is forwarded to the frontend container's own nginx, which
# already proxies /api/ and /uploads/ to the backend internally - so this
# only needs one upstream, not one entry per service.
ppsl.net.in {
	tls /etc/caddy/certs/ppsl_net_in.pem /etc/caddy/certs/ppsl_net_in.key
	reverse_proxy frontend:80
}

# Once you've also added a DNS A record for www.ppsl.net.in pointing at
# the same IP, add this block too so www redirects to the root domain
# instead of failing to resolve. A Cloudflare Origin Certificate covers
# both ppsl.net.in and *.ppsl.net.in if you included the wildcard
# hostname when creating it, so no separate cert is needed for this:
#
# www.ppsl.net.in {
# 	tls /etc/caddy/certs/ppsl_net_in.pem /etc/caddy/certs/ppsl_net_in.key
# 	redir https://ppsl.net.in{uri} permanent
# }
